/-!
# Strict homogeneous master certificates

Strict (`0 < P`) companions of the five Bernstein interval certs in `HomogMaster.lean`.
Each `P` is the `(T - GS)`-shaped certificate integrand; the non-strict cert proves
`0 <= P` on `[lo, hi]` via the Bernstein decomposition `P = sum c_i (mu-lo)^i (hi-mu)^(d-i)`
with every `c_i > 0`.  Here we upgrade to strict `0 < P` on the *whole* closed interval:
on `mu < hi` the leading term `c_0 (hi-mu)^d > 0`; at `mu = hi` the trailing term
`c_d (mu-lo)^d > 0` (since `lo < hi`).  The nonneg `t_i` haves and the `ring` identity are
verbatim from the non-strict cert; only the final conclusion is strengthened.
Kernel-clean: axioms = [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound].
-/

